  "title": "Alexander the Great",
  "summary": "Alexander III of Macedon was born at Pella in 356 BCE and became king in 336 BCE. His campaign took him through Asia Minor, to the battles at the Granicus, Issus and Gaugamela, and east to the Hydaspes in India, where he defeated King Porus in 326 BCE. He died in Babylon in June 323 BCE, after which his empire was divided among his generals.",
